<p>Two U.S. service members were reported missing May 2 near the Cap Draa Training Area outside Tan-Tan in southwestern Morocco after taking part in African Lion, U.S. Africa Command’s annual multinational military exercise. A U.S. defense official told The Associated Press the two were Army soldiers who went missing while hiking after the day’s exercises ended. U.S., Moroccan and other partner forces began coordinated search-and-rescue operations with ground, air and maritime assets.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/cLmi7ffCVDqfd-k6L-E8dK1TIKXmg7kDWr7FFnLUsq8V-qOsEMdHd6CFtFXsvrk2mb21Rqo89ZXZf4qkl3NU-NmhVu6Q9w-lkKBvUWYFleDpx7yZlovH7M7LD0i8MyFxjvGkFh7vYSU8kczZJe3ssPLYq8fPFi_HXms' alt='U.S. soldiers and Royal Moroccan Army soldiers fast-rope during the African Lion exercise in 2021.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Exercise scale: Morocco is hosting the largest portion of African Lion 2026, with about 5,000 personnel from more than 40 countries; the wider exercise also spans Ghana, Senegal and Tunisia.</li><li>Incident status: U.S. Africa Command and the Moroccan Royal Armed Forces said the circumstances remained under investigation.</li><li>Training focus: A U.S. Army description cited by JNS says the exercise focuses on joint all-domain operations, crisis response and readiness for crises and contingencies.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>U.S. Africa Command: AFRICOM said its priority was the service members involved and their families. (<a href='https://www.eldiario.es/internacional/desaparecidos-militares-estadounidenses-durante-maniobras-internacionales-conjuntas-marruecos_1_13191575.html'>elDiario.es</a>)</li><li>Moroccan Royal Armed Forces: Moroccan forces said the soldiers were reported missing at 9 p.m. local time in a cliff area of Cap Draa. (<a href='https://www.eldiario.es/internacional/desaparecidos-militares-estadounidenses-durante-maniobras-internacionales-conjuntas-marruecos_1_13191575.html'>elDiario.es</a>)</li><li>U.S. defense offici